{
  "description": "Handwritten #243 and #252 paging witnesses. The complete original inventory travels as a bounded top index (per original revision: its field count and the SHA-256 and canonical byte length of its revision field index, plus the SHA-256 of the canonical JSON of revisions); each revision field index (ordered names and declaration digests) and the declarations arrive in read-port pages bound to the collection revision and inventory digest. items are the declaration pages the cases serve by cursor; fieldIndexes are the revision field index pages they serve by entry (fieldIndexPages, default [0,1]); a case with its own index serves every page under that index's digest; fieldIndexRequests are the exact requests of the successful case; inventory, index, changedInventory and changedIndex are the host collection before and after a change during preview. bounds are the #252 bound proof: an inventory generator gives revision r (from 0) the label issue-252 'prep_'+32 'c'+':recipe:'+(r+1) or max 156 'r' + r as 4 digits (160 bytes), field f the name issue-252 'f'+61 'a'+f as 2 digits (64 bytes) or wide 157 'w'+f as 3 digits (160 bytes), and fieldJson {\"name\":<name>,\"description\":\"r\"+(r+1) as at least 3 digits,\"type\":\"text\"}; a top generator gives entry r the label 157 U+0001 followed by three characters from the 27 control characters other than U+0008, U+0009, U+000A, U+000C and U+000D (index r in base 27, most significant first), the stated fields and bytes (label, when given, replaces the generated label of every entry), and digest 'sha256:'+'ab' x 32. indexBytes, fieldIndexBytes and oneLevelIndexBytes (the #250 one-level index) are canonical byte lengths. Digests and lengths were computed outside the package. Go and TypeScript drive both factories through every case.",
